<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Edict of Pîtres</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">864</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Edict of Pîtres was a set of laws issued by the West Frankish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a> at an assembly at Pîtres on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seine">Seine</a> in June 864. It reformed the coinage, ordering a standard <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> penny struck at a limited number of mints, and ordered fortified bridges on the rivers to stop <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> raiders from sailing inland. It also forbade the sale of weapons and horses to the Vikings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/edict-of-pitres.jpg" alt="Edict of Pîtres" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Numisantica · CC BY-SA 3.0 nl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charles_the_Bald_denier_struck_Reims.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
